\cf1 ##HelpTopicID=111\cf0\par
\cf1 ##HelpTopicID=112\cf0\par
The \b Tap and Drag\b0  features duplicate the functionality of the "mouse" buttons.\par
\par
\b Tap again and hold to drag\b0\par
Select this check box to drag objects without pressing the mouse or TouchPad button. To drag, tap twice on the object and keep your finger down on the TouchPad on the second tap. Move the selected object by sliding your finger across the TouchPad surface and lift your finger to drop the object.\par
\par
\b Locking Drags\b0\par
The \b Locking Drags\b0  feature allows objects to be dragged long distances across the screen using several finger strokes. When \b Locking Drags\b0  is selected, a drag action persists after you lift your finger from the TouchPad. Tap the TouchPad again to drop the object and end the drag. To use \b Locking Drags\b0 , the \b Tap again and hold to drag\b0  feature must also be selected.\par
\par
\cf1 ##HelpTopicID=113\cf0\par
The \b Virtual Scrolling\b0  feature allows you to scroll with a single stroke of your finger. Virtual Scrolling operates the scroll bars automatically so there is no need to move the pointer away from your work. Virtual Scrolling works with most scrollable windows such as word processing documents, spreadsheets, and large digital images. It also works with other scrollable items such as file lists and font lists. Virtual Scrolling provides the easiest and smoothest scrolling for all applications.\par
\par
Click on the window or item you wish to scroll and slide your finger up and down the right edge of the TouchPad to scroll vertically.\par
\par
To enable this feature, select the \b Enable vertical scrolling\b0  or \b Enable horizontal scrolling\b0  check box.\par
\par
If Virtual Scrolling does not respond, ensure that the desired \b Enable scrolling\b0  check box is selected and that the window or item you have clicked on is scrollable. If you still have problems, check your \b Scrolling Region\b0  settings.\par
\par
\cf1 ##HelpTopicID=114\cf0\par
The \b Sensitivity\b0  settings allow you to personalize the way the TouchPad responds to your touch. To adjust the Sensitivity settings, select an item from the \b Sensitivity\b0  menu tree.\par
\par
