\cf1 ##HelpTopicID=119\cf0\par
The \b Sticky Borders\b0  feature restricts the pointer to stay inside the active window. When you try to move the pointer outside the window, it stops at the edge. If you try a second time, the pointer is free to leave the window.\par
\par
Stopping the pointer at the window borders makes it easy to access controls that lie around the edges of a window. For example, to close or resize a window, you can quickly move the pointer in the general direction of the close box or the edge of the window, and the pointer will stop exactly where you want.\par
\par
To enable this feature, select the \b Enable sticky borders\b0  check box.\par
\par
